Package: ldfreq
Type: Package
Title: Reproducible Lexical Diversity and Frequency Profiles
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person(
        given = "Ryuya",
        family = "Komuro",
        email = "komuro.4121@gmail.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
Description: Compares lexical diversity and reference-vocabulary profiles while
    retaining the formula, parameters, preprocessing choices, and match coverage
    used in each analysis. Computes twelve lexical-diversity measures from
    ordered tokens or raw English text; compares selected Maas and MTLD
    definitions; and exposes local MATTR windows. Bundled New JACET 8000 and
    TUBELEX tables support lexical-level coverage and corpus-relative frequency
    profiles, with off-list terms and non-computable requests kept explicit.
    Additional functions provide exact lexical overlap, reference-set coverage,
    caller-supplied lexical norm profiles, multi-document workflows, and plots.
    The methods include Covington and McFall (2010)
    <doi:10.1080/09296171003643098> and McCarthy and Jarvis (2010)
    <doi:10.3758/BRM.42.2.381>.
